  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "↵Fiddler is my favorite debugging proxy on Windows.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "my-fiddler-cookbook",
        "title": "My Fiddler Cookbook",
        "url": "/blog/my-fiddler-cookbook/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Usually, I use Python to write simple debugging proxy which is usually less than 30 lines until it needs https.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "my-fiddler-cookbook",
        "title": "My Fiddler Cookbook",
        "url": "/blog/my-fiddler-cookbook/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "That's why my first configuration on Fiddler is Decrypting HTTPS traffic,",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "my-fiddler-cookbook",
        "title": "My Fiddler Cookbook",
        "url": "/blog/my-fiddler-cookbook/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Check Decrypt HTTPS traffic and click OK.↵",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "my-fiddler-cookbook",
        "title": "My Fiddler Cookbook",
        "url": "/blog/my-fiddler-cookbook/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It will then ask to install a Trust Root Certificate,↵ ↵",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "my-fiddler-cookbook",
        "title": "My Fiddler Cookbook",
        "url": "/blog/my-fiddler-cookbook/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The scary text is a warning about https traffic being seen by Fiddler.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "my-fiddler-cookbook",
        "title": "My Fiddler Cookbook",
        "url": "/blog/my-fiddler-cookbook/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Fiddler's root certificate is now trusted, which means Fiddler can generate certificates trusted by your applications, including your browser.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "my-fiddler-cookbook",
        "title": "My Fiddler Cookbook",
        "url": "/blog/my-fiddler-cookbook/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "If it doesn't prompt you to install the certificate, you can have the certificate installed with below,↵",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "my-fiddler-cookbook",
        "title": "My Fiddler Cookbook",
        "url": "/blog/my-fiddler-cookbook/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "You can run a very simple load test by selecting multiple request, and then press R.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "my-fiddler-cookbook",
        "title": "My Fiddler Cookbook",
        "url": "/blog/my-fiddler-cookbook/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Beware the response from the server may be cached in different layer of the infrastructure.↵",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "my-fiddler-cookbook",
        "title": "My Fiddler Cookbook",
        "url": "/blog/my-fiddler-cookbook/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "You can see how well the servers perform from the Timeline.↵",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "my-fiddler-cookbook",
        "title": "My Fiddler Cookbook",
        "url": "/blog/my-fiddler-cookbook/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Sometimes you can even see the number of outgoing connection limit on Windows by checking with Timeline.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "my-fiddler-cookbook",
        "title": "My Fiddler Cookbook",
        "url": "/blog/my-fiddler-cookbook/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "You can also modify your request before sending it out,↵ ↵",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "my-fiddler-cookbook",
        "title": "My Fiddler Cookbook",
        "url": "/blog/my-fiddler-cookbook/"
      }
    }
  ],
